   "l": "one who clasps well does not come loose,",
   "v": true,
   "i": "clasp well, and it does not slip away;",
   "n": "脫 is intransitive — a thing slips loose, rather than a man letting go of it — and the subject here is the man, so the literal above lets him come loose rather than lose his grip. The same verb held the fish in chapter 36: 魚不可脫於淵, the fish cannot slip out of the deep."
