   "l": "Cultivate it in the person —\nits potency then genuine;\ncultivate it in the household —\nits potency then running over;",
   "v": true,
   "i": "Cultivate it in your own person, and its potency is the real thing; cultivate it in the household, and its potency runs over;",
   "n": "之 is the object pronoun again, and what is cultivated is never named — the Way, understood from the whole book. Chinese drops whatever can be guessed.\n\n乃 is the ladder-word from chapter 16's 容乃公，公乃全: 'and then, and so it follows'. Here it builds a different ladder, upward through the circles a man belongs to — his own person, his household, and in the next unit his district, his state, all under heaven. Each rung is the one below it written large, and the rungs are the standard furniture of Warring States political thought."
  },
