   "l": "By what do I know that all under heaven is so?\nBy this.",
   "v": true,
   "i": "How do I know that all under heaven is so? By this.",
   "n": "何以 is 以何 with the question word pulled to the front — an interrogative pronoun always goes before the word that governs it, never after. Chapter 21 closed on the same two lines with a different object, and chapter 13's 何謂寵辱若驚 is the same rule again.\n\n然 is 'so, thus, being-so' — the same 然 that makes 自然 'so of itself' in chapter 51.\n\n'By this' — by what? By the ladder just climbed: by looking at each thing through its own kind. The book likes to end a chapter by pointing rather than explaining."
